Task 1 — Part of #1021 / #1037 (product). Users on google, xai and mistral who pick gemini-4-argon, gemini-3.8-flash, grok-4.7 or mistral-large-4 get guessed limits and no /cost price today. yoagent 0.25.8 already ships proper presets for those four, so this task wires them in.
• Exact id match only. Lookalikes such as gemini-3.8-flash-lite stay on the generic settings, so a variant isn't billed at its base model's rate.
• First step is checking the premise. The assessment only searched for the id strings, so the implementer must confirm these ids really fall through to the generic code today.
• Files: the code goes in agent_builder.rs and providers.rs. Tests go in a new provider_presets_tests.rs, because agent_builder.rs is 60 lines below its size limit.
• Docs: the doc comment and models.md get a note that three of these presets carry the regular rate, so /cost may read up to 2× during Google's and Mistral's promotion.
• Out of scope: changing each provider's default model, the zai/qwen presets, and removing the stale gemini-3.0 ids.

Task 2 — Fixes #1047 (product). In config_paths.rs, the two reads of the trusted-dirs file go through the existing safe reader (non_regular_read).
• Checking whether a directory is trusted: this runs at startup, so a FIFO at that path currently hangs yoyo before the first turn. After the fix, a file it can't read counts as "not trusted", so an unreadable store never grants trust.
• Saving a trusted directory: today an unreadable file is treated as empty and overwritten, which would wipe every trusted directory. After the fix it refuses to write instead.
• Stale doc sentence: non_regular_read.rs still says yoagent 0.25.7's read tool doesn't check for non-regular files; 0.25.8 made that false, so it gets rewritten. The other 0.25.7 mentions get re-checked in the same change.
• Before the push: the title says "Fixes", which closes #1047. So the implementer must update every #1047 mention in the code and docs, and file a new issue for any other startup read that skips the safe reader.

